  "strayReplyRouting": "A worker replying to a `from` socket that nobody listens on does not fail silently — the CLI delivers the reply to another registered peer. Measured by accident: the probe advertised a socket it never bound, and every reply landed in the one other registered peer on the machine. relay registers as a peer, so it WILL receive replies addressed to nobody. Two consequences: relay must listen on the socket it advertises as `from`, and ingest must drop inbound frames that do not resolve to one of its own tasks.",
  "replyFrameShape": "{msgV:1, msg_id:<fresh>, type, message:{role,content}, priority:'next', from:'uds:/tmp/cc-socks/<sender pid>.sock'} with the text wrapped as <cross-session-message from=… hop-chain=… from-name=… from-mode=…>. No session id and no in-reply-to: resolve the sender via from → ~/.claude/sessions/<pid>.json → sessionId (from-name is not an identity — spike ⑦ measured two live sessions sharing a name). hop-chain is stable across a chain and absent on the first reply — a loop-detection id, never a message key."
}
